              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MARSKYGIRL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really liked this sauce, but made a couple small changes too. Like many others, I added about 1/4 teaspoon sugar to the sauce. I also changed the minced garlic to garlic powder, with good results. Use this with the \"Pizza Crust for Bread Machine\" recipe on this site for a quick and easy home-made pizza dinner!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mauxjen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect tomato sauce for pizza! I added some Italian seasoning as well. I pour the sauce into ice cube trays and freeze, then pop them into a freezer bag. I then make individual pizzas with naan and microwave one individual sauce cube per pizza. Add toppings and mozza and into the air fryer for ten minutes. Perfect and inexpensive!",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-19T04:33:06.614Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tobreth Hansen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We usually make sauce from stewed tomatoes. I wanted to use up this little bit of tomato sauce, so I tried this. I followed the recipe BUT I cooked it down to thicken it and take away the canned taste, and I used a little extra garlic and some garlic infused olive oil.",
            "datePublished": "2020-09-15T16:39:48.037Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shanlee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The quickest, easiest and tastiest pizza sauce I have ever made! This is easily adaptable to what you have on hand. If you don't have fresh garlic or don't feel like mincing, substitute 1/4 tsp garlic powder. If you don't have oregano and basil separately, substitute 1 tsp Italian Seasoning. I also like to add 1/2 tsp sugar as other reviewers suggested. Use as the pizza sauce called for in any recipe. My favorite is the \"Pizza Rolls\" from this site.",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-22T00:59:59.083Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dickisonfamily"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Doubled the seasoning, added 1 TBS brown sugar. Covered 2, 9x13 pizzas. Used on quick and easy pizza crust recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2017-11-21T05:27:06.633Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
