            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naturelover"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like to use a large fresh tomato diced small, minced garlic, and a tablespoon of olive oil and oregano for my pizza sauce. If I don't have fresh tomatoes available this is a great, quick substitute.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-21T11:37:10.483Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jill75"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very simple and good. I used on some French bread pizza, using my own canned tomato sauce. I did add 1/4 t. sugar, 1 t of Italian seasoning and substituted garlic powder for the minced garlic. I liked that it uses ingredients that I have on hand and super-fast to whip up! Thank you for sharing!",
            "datePublished": "2025-02-09T23:00:12.705Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
